  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Onboard: on the phone",
      "items": [
        "MediaPipe Tasks Vision in the page, on the GPU when it can: BlazeFace for faces, EfficientDet-Lite0 for COCO's 80 objects, the gesture recogniser for hands (see.js 58–72). Measured on the ANE-LX1: faces 85 ms, hands 212 ms; \"what is this?\" 2.6 s, reading 2.7 s.",
        "js-aruco2 for markers (distance and angle from their printed size), its own colour finder, the browser's BarcodeDetector for QR codes (see.js 83–88, 131, 240–242); Tesseract.js reads text in German, English and French and the phone says it (omi.js 175–199).",
        "The eyes follow the nearest face on the phone itself, at 4 looks a second while they hold one, 1 while nobody is there (see.js 20–21, 322–326)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Edge: on the Pi",
      "items": [
        "The Pi gets numbers, never pixels: parse() keeps known fields and clamps them; faces go out at most 10 a second, other kinds at MAX_SEE_RATE (protocol.py 129–262, bridge_node.py 383–398).",
        "The Desk Guardian decides on them: a face wakes it, the Thymio turns to it, the owner's QR card makes a friend (guardian.py 28–39, 133–147). Omi Assist asks for faces only, with following, and greets a face after five minutes alone (omi_assist.py 26–29, 85–91)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Kept back",
      "items": [
        "Telling faces apart is face-api's 128-number signature, in the page's memory for this session only; the bridge sets the number to null unless the facilitator allowed it (see.js 137–140, bridge_node.py 388).",
        "Reading and \"what is this?\" send only line counts and a label (contract.py 44–45). A heavier model on the Pi would need the pictures to leave the phone; a camera of the Pi's own would be the way (not built). In Webots the twin's Recognition stands in for these models."
      ]
    }
  ]
